XDJ-RX patch 18: auth coprocessor on I2C4 (fixes E-7206) + sub-ucom version word.

E-7206 "AUTH CHIP ERROR": the guest kernel has a 4th i.MX6 I2C controller,
imx-i2c.3 at 0x021F8000 (/dev/i2c-3), carrying an Apple MFi authentication
coprocessor at slave 0x10. QEMU's i.MX6 models only I2C1-3, so the chip never
answered. rbp's startup self-check (FUN_00349294) writes register pointer 0x00 and
reads 1 byte that must be 0x05 (Device Version, CP 2.0C), then register 0x01 that
must be 0x01 (Firmware Version); a NACK or other value -> E-7206.
Adds an IMX I2C controller at 0x021F8000 (GIC SPI 35, mapped over the catch-all)
and an I2C slave "xdj-mfi-cp" at 0x10 answering the identity registers (version,
firmware, protocol 2.0, device ID 0x00000200; everything else reads 0). It does not
sign challenges or carry a certificate -- only needed when an iPod connects.
Verified: self-check returns 0 (gdb at 0x34932c), I2C4 IRQ counts, UI clean.

Sub-ucom version word: frame bytes 2-3 are the panel MCU firmware version (LE).
rbp keeps it from the first frame (FUN_00282630 -> +0x94) and test mode prints it
as "SUB Ver.%x.%02x". The real MCU reports 0.35 (images/subucom.rev); we sent 0.
Default 0x0035, override XDJ_SUBUCOM_VER=<hex>.

